class:: ModalPlateModel
summary:: Kirchhoff-Love simply supported rectangular plate preparation
categories:: UGens>Reverbs, Libraries>CamaraObscura
related:: Guides/CamaraObscura, Classes/ModalPlate

description::

ModalPlateModel derives rectangular-plate modes from the Kirchhoff-Love thin
plate equation. Frequencies use flexural rigidity, density, thickness,
dimensions, and simply supported integer mode pairs. The payload also stores
frequency-dependent damping and normalized mode-shape factors.

Only code::\simplySupported:: boundaries are implemented. Runtime pitch and
drive are artistic scalings and are not claimed as nonlinear plate tension.
The closest vanilla class is link::Classes/Klank::, but this model derives
resonances and moving spatial participation from physical parameters rather
than accepting an arbitrary frequency table.

classmethods::

method:: rectangular
Prepare a simply supported plate.

argument:: width
Plate width in metres.

argument:: height
Plate height in metres.

argument:: thickness
Plate thickness in metres.

argument:: density
Material density in kilograms per cubic metre.

argument:: youngModulus
Young's modulus in pascals.

argument:: poissonRatio
Poisson ratio greater than -0.999 and below 0.499.

argument:: damping
Positive proportional damping coefficient used to derive modal T60.

argument:: modes
Maximum retained modes below 0.49 times sample rate, from 1 through 4096.

argument:: boundary
Only code::\simplySupported::.

argument:: sampleRate
Exact renderer sample rate.

method:: read
Read a version-1 plate model.

instancemethods::

method:: validate
Validate metadata, integer mode pairs, Nyquist bounds, damping, and
normalization data.

method:: summary
Return concise diagnostics.

method:: load
Upload to a mono Buffer.

method:: write
Serialize the model.

method:: free
Free the last uploaded Buffer.

method:: plotModes
Plot the derived frequencies.

method:: plotShape
Plot one ideal simply supported sin-sin mode shape.

method:: plotResponse
Plot modal frequencies.

examples::

code::
(
var steel = ModalPlateModel.rectangular(
    1.8, 1.0, 0.0005, 7850,
    2e11, 0.3, 0.012,
    modes: 256, sampleRate: 48000
);
steel.summary.postln;
steel.plotModes;
)
::

code::
(
var plate = ModalPlateModel.rectangular(
    1.2, 0.8, 0.0007, 2700,
    6.9e10, 0.33, 0.02,
    modes: 128, sampleRate: 48000
);
plate.plotShape(5);
)
::

